  title "Bone that Bleeds"
  summary "☽'tenebris, a fire-core practitioner, repeatedly fails to extend conduit burn cycles because bone-lattice inevitably fractures under thermal expansion stress. After consulting with Cevmucsiatum-larv~, who reads the deep-ice memory of the original workshop, she discovers that the ancient Luminary's maker solved this problem by using corrupted ice-stone housings with porous bone-lattice lined with living fungal cultures that metabolize excess heat. ☽'tenebris successfully replicates this design, creating a self-sustaining thermal cycle where fungi feed on the fire-core's heat and bleed residual energy into the seepage, allowing a conduit to burn steadily for twelve hours without fracturing—matching the impossible endurance of the legendary Luminary."
